# Explicit config for core's generalized record-fields gate (core issue #66).
# Role-unique value only — the checking logic itself now lives in core.
# Per docs/issue-1/proposals/security-threat-model.md (b): risk-rating scheme
# (CVSS-style qualitative severity default; DREAD-style override permitted
# only for architectural/trust-boundary findings with no CVE-like vector,
# marked inline) lives inside stride-table/residual-risk-note cells, not as
# its own gated field — the gate below only checks field presence.
RECORD_FIELDS_REQUIRED="asset-inventory,trust-boundary-map,stride-table,mitigation-list,residual-risk-note,canon-references"

# No terminal-loop_state divergence exists for this role (issue-20) from the
# marketplace's 4-state set named in roles/specs/security-threat-model
# .spec.json / roles/security-threat-model.json (tokenmaxxxer/on-the-record):
# modeling (progress), landed (terminal), trust-boundary-undetermined
# (refusal), spec-unreadable (error). RECORD_FIELDS_TERMINAL_STATES is
# intentionally unset here. Add it using the same explicit-named-config
# pattern if a role-specific terminal state set is ever needed.
